<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nocera Inferiore</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nocera Inferiore is a town in the province of Salerno, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/campania">Campania</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, in the Sarno valley. It stands on the site of ancient Nuceria Alfaterna, head of a league of towns that became an ally of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> after 308 BCE; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal</a> destroyed it in 216 BCE. In 59 CE a riot between Nucerians and Pompeians in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompeii">Pompeii</a>'s amphitheatre, recorded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tacitus">Tacitus</a>, led the Senate to ban games at Pompeii for ten years.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nocera-inferiore.jpg" alt="Nocera Inferiore" width="320" height="259" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Giaros Original uploader was Nuceria5 at it.wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nocera_Inferiore_pos_SA.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
